    "narrative": "For this August 31st slate, our offensive core is headlined by **Bryce Harper** (71.42) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47), both of whom benefit significantly from facing Brandon Pfaadt and Robert Stock, respectively. **Bryce Harper** is our must-start today, bolstered by a strong .394 xwOBA and a favorable slot in the #3 hole against Pfaadt. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** receives a massive +19% boost from the SP skill of Stock, turning him into a high-ceiling anchor at 1B. While **Luis Arraez** (66.78) is also a strong play, we are keeping a close eye on **Dylan Beavers** (65.51). **Dylan Beavers** is a critical asset today; his score is elevated by a +14% park factor and a +4% boost for his stolen base potential against Tanner Gordon\u2019s slow delivery\u2014a mandatory selection given our need to stay competitive in the SB category.\n\nOur bench strategy was razor-thin today, with **Braden Montgomery** (47.20) falling just short of the cut. **Braden Montgomery** actually projected slightly better than **Gleyber Torres** (46.98), but **Gleyber Torres** secured the final MI spot due to the high-leverage utility of his projected leadoff position. We are exercising caution with several assignments, most notably **Lawrence Butler**, who faces the daunting task of squaring off against Jacob deGrom. While **Lawrence Butler** carries a respectable 51.34, his efficiency is cannibalized by a -19% penalty against deGrom\u2019s elite repertoire. Furthermore, please note that all lineups remain \"Pending\" as of this writing; if **Cal Raleigh** (59.37) or **Jung Hoo Lee** (61.02) are dropped down their respective batting orders once official cards are posted, their scores will see an immediate downward correction. Be advised that **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains unavailable due to a scheduled team off-day, limiting our options for high-end power production today.",
